# Line endings are part of the test fixtures.
#
# `tests/fixtures/kitchen-sink.md` is compiled into the test binaries with
# `include_str!`, so its bytes *are* the input: tests index into it, search it
# for markers, and compare byte offsets against the source ranges the renderer
# reports. A checkout that turns its newlines into CRLF changes every offset
# past the first line and makes a pattern spanning two lines match nothing —
# which is exactly how a green suite failed on the Windows runner alone.
#
# The same applies to every other file read verbatim at compile time: the
# README and `docs/KEYBINDINGS.md` (`tests/docs.rs` matches text in both),
# `Cargo.toml`, and the bundled themes.
#
# Nothing here wants CRLF — there are no batch or PowerShell files, and the
# shell scripts, PKGBUILDs and nix derivation would break with it — so the
# rule is simply LF everywhere, in the repository and in the working tree on
# every platform. Git decides what is text by content; the exceptions below
# name the binaries it should not inspect at all.
* text=auto eol=lf

*.gif binary
*.png binary
